less for OpenVMS
================

This is less @VERSION@, the pager, built natively for OpenVMS @ARCH@, from
the unmodified release plus the patches in the vms-less project:

    https://github.com/issinoho/vms-less

Kit version: @KITVERSION@.  less is free software under the GNU General
Public License, version 3 or later, or the Less License; see COPYING.  The
manual is LESS.1, also as plain text in LESS.TXT.

Files
-----
    LESS$ROOT:[BIN]LESS.EXE
    LESS$ROOT:[DOC]                     this file, COPYING, NEWS, the manual
    LESS$ROOT:[000000]LESS$SETUP.COM    defines the less command
    SYS$STARTUP:LESS$STARTUP.COM        defines LESS$ROOT

Setup
-----
The kit installs LESS$STARTUP.COM into SYS$STARTUP and runs it once.  To
define LESS$ROOT at every boot, the system manager adds this line to
SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM:

    $ @SYS$STARTUP:LESS$STARTUP.COM

Each user then defines the command (for example in LOGIN.COM):

    $ @LESS$ROOT:[000000]LESS$SETUP.COM

Use
---
    $ less LOGIN.COM
    $ pipe directory/full | less
